<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting — MorphoEval overall 91.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py` (91.1/100, up from 56.8/100 in Pass 1; +34.3 points). The remediated script implements all 4 canonical phase regimes of Graner & Glazier (1992) and Glazier & Graner (1993) (`complete_sorting_engulfment`, `partial_sorting_lens`, `checkerboard_mixing`, and `cell_dissociation`) plus `zero_temp_pinning_control` (`T = 0`) and `equal_adhesion_control` (`gamma_LD = 0`), executes a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep and a 6-point temperature sweep (`T in {0, 1.5, 5, 10, 25, 80}`), verifies logarithmic boundary decay (`r = -0.9459`, PRL Fig. 3 checkpoint `r = 0.9724`), segments the SHA-256-locked confocal embryonic cell aggregate specimen (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`, radial profile `r = 0.9612, RMSE = 0.154`), and is backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_042_cellular_potts_cell_sorting.lean`. Overall 91.2/100 (faithfulness 90.8, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py at b9976f8, image/png, 625763 B, 3000×1260 px, artifact_sha256 94cf7dc29ecf10cff051dd93ee95b5ee2557e2bab5b85948a912a902322f4ffe (sha256 94cf7dc29ecf10cff051dd93ee95b5ee2557e2bab5b85948a912a902322f4ffe), spec_fingerprint 7cdd3f38f0e6192e614f25f3f47d81cb4d09870705b0e0dca1d1d4dbca9f4cc0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7cdd3f38f0e6192e614f25f3f47d81cb4d09870705b0e0dca1d1d4dbca9f4cc0; artifact_sha256: 94cf7dc29ecf10cff051dd93ee95b5ee2557e2bab5b85948a912a902322f4ffe. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t). | Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting).; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep. | Computer-vision segmentation of confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.9612, RMSE = 0.154).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections.; does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover or active chemotactic signaling.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the 2D Cellular Potts Hamiltonian to include a perimeter elasticity constraint lambda_P * (p_sigma - P_t)^2 for explicit cortical tension modeling." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.12e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

